"""Thirteen complete gate/certificate/support owners; manual semantic assessments."""
import json,pathlib,runpy
H=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent;P='additional_rust_ooutwire_remaining';p=H/(P+'_notes.json');n=json.loads(p.read_text())
rows={
24:('All189 budget lines, including exact shared-template transfer and World tests, reviewed.','checked_sub correctly refuses zero and charges one per accepted response. Copyable local u32 fuel is not a durable money ledger or a bound on proposal/search work. Funding provenance is outside this representation.'),
41:('All207 license lines, gates/tests and exact shared-template transfers reviewed.','License is a public Boolean event-backed state, independent of fuel; structural responses require it and instance-only repairs do not. The file explicitly leaves grantor authority unmodeled. It provides neither identity authentication nor external permission verification.'),
45:('Complete215 menu lines and tests reviewed with exact template reconstruction.','menu validates supported bounds and enumerates cost0..max_items unpruned. Public mutable items and space strings do not authenticate complete enumeration; same data/form counts produce identical SpaceId for structurally different bases. Source tests check count/composition, not all possible base invariants.'),
56:('All212 repair lines reviewed, including finite filter, partition methods and tests.','Soundness/completeness is exactly relative to supplied menu and response_valid_naive; repairs versus augmentations is a shape partition. Invalid candidates/errors become false and examined counts include them. No proof of menu origin, well-formedness or coverage is carried by the public type.'),
48:('All218 obstruction lines reviewed with exact template transfer.','Positive guard requires a recorded currently violated pair; exhaustive failure is relative to the supplied Menu. An empty forged menu yields an Exhaustion record even when a true menu has repairs. World recomputes its own menu before accepting refusal, so this is a public record/API trust boundary rather than a demonstrated World bypass.'),
28:('All278 certificate lines, kind/display code, tests and compile-fail source reviewed.','Three sum-type variants prevent confusing kinds in pattern matching; no From<TestResult> is a useful API distinction. Public payloads are explicitly declaration records, not proof objects. String object/check/proof IDs and examined counts bind no actual witness or domain; zero-sum example only refutes exact-opposite pairing, not general cancellation.'),
53:('All208 refusal lines and represented-refusal tests reviewed with exact template transfer.','Refusal is a persistent record, not an absorbing terminal. Source tests exercise mismatched payload rejection, recomputed bounded exhaustion and later wider response. Actual guard belongs to world.rs; historical record can outlive changed bounds or repaired targets and is not a fresh impossibility theorem.'),
50:('All229 panel lines, guards and tests reviewed with exact shared-template transfer.','Nonempty panel and well-formed ordered target/contexts are enforced. Positive unanimity means each evaluator has some separating column; negative unanimity concerns only the union of their columns. Blind empty-context evaluators give negative agreement despite global separation. No correspondence, observer adequacy or truth follows from unanimity.'),
61:('Complete145 scope lines reviewed without elision.','Scope is mutable metadata, not a proof of actual search or source binding. SealedScopeWitness checks nonempty strings and two distinct named measures only; it does not validate bounds, reading identity, population truth or immutable coupling to Scope. Mutation-count prose was not executed.'),
69:('Complete406 World lines, every event branch, response/refusal guard and tests reviewed with exact template transfer.','Response requires recorded violated target, ordered bounded delta, valid separation and all requirements, fuel and structure license. Refusal rebuilds menu and equality-checks certificate, closing caller-forged-menu path. Carrier admissions explicitly bypass response gates. Unsupported bounds return Refused, but allocations/exponential contexts/panics preclude unconditional machine totality; one external bounds value governs entire replay and is not itself an event.'),
64:('All217 Support lines and tests reviewed with exact shared-template reconstruction.','Exhaustive World destructuring forces a source change when fields are added; notes are explicitly excluded. Inspection of current step branches supports factorization through support for fixed event/bounds, apart from machine resources. Seven-event tests are examples, not exhaustive proof, and discarded notes still affect memory/copy costs.'),
65:('All333 terminal lines, all verdict branches and tests reviewed with exact template reconstruction.','DeclaredTerminalizer accurately documents mapping caller declarations, not independent checking. Nonempty witness strings suffice for Accepted and only certificate kind is checked for Refused. Public enum/Terminated fields make never-bare prose a usage convention, not encapsulation. Engine provenance must establish stronger claims.'),
66:('All101 testkit lines reviewed.','cfg(test) constructors and legacy edge-string parser support replay tests. Separate checked parser enforces ASCII digits, checked usize arithmetic, exact formatting and distinctness but is not used by edge_events, which still unwraps strings and treats supply name specially. Test-only API; no production parser hardening claim.')}
for i,(a,l)in rows.items():n[str(i)]={'assessment':a,'limitations':l}
p.write_text(json.dumps(n,indent=2)+'\n');runpy.run_path(str(H/(P+'_checkpoint.py')));runpy.run_path(str(H/(P+'_synthesis03.py')))
